        "question": {
          ":question/id": "8253f676-2b14-5906-9ca1-ca29b8dcdab7",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $3$ rows and $3$ columns, so it is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- $B$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $4$ rows and $4$ columns, so it is a $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- $C$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $4$ rows and $1$ column, so it's a $4\\times 1$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are square matrices.",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
